{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731254Z","id":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.905107Z","id":"e345bb553d4e3e680daad70f7c5d05ec91d0b38821fb38154b5e3ce95f874fef","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","supersedes":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.151745Z","id":"3f266ae83272f0220b862e118174c5b0b9fdeaf0aa0c63d555a38f5e193522f9","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","supersedes":"e345bb553d4e3e680daad70f7c5d05ec91d0b38821fb38154b5e3ce95f874fef","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752276Z","id":"a4e0fc3d2449cef6e4c9e5c62dbf3e8fb48354924f9738b81f8f488f38ead924","body":{"detail":"The tests in web/bridge/test/long-press.test.ts and comment-mode.test.ts dispatch synthetic TouchEvents in jsdom. Three browser behaviours they cannot show: (1) that the cancelled touchend still grants the frame user activation, which the shell requires before it takes clax:pick-start (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.5); (2) that Android Chrome/WebView still delivers touchend, not touchcancel, after the long-press contextmenu that comment-mode.ts cancels; (3) that no click is synthesized after the cancelled touchend (comment-mode.ts swallows one within 800 ms in case it is).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"571b41cf4f06dcc085a48acdbdbb6ab4e2f8e92aa64da6e4cecd98a8a433efd1"},"suggested_fix":"Exercise a long-press in the Playwright app-mode e2e with touch emulation (hasTouch) and on an Android device or emulator, and confirm a composer opens with a clip.","summary":"Long-press pick on a real Android WebView is unverified: activation, contextmenu and touchcancel","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752447Z","id":"e941822a7ca1c95d030d297f6a807ef7f3fddb5f5be19dda259c85474a638073","body":{"detail":"While the document is too short to reach y, restoreScroll retries every 100 ms for up to 2000 ms and then scrolls to y. If the viewer scrolls the new version during that wait, the restore still moves the page under them once the document grows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"976d3a24272d77f4d4c99c457071ba7ccbbcea345f4836021a184237edf283ff"},"suggested_fix":"Stop the retries on a trusted wheel, touchmove or keydown in the page before the restore lands.","summary":"restoreScroll does not yield to the viewer's own scroll while it waits","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752506Z","id":"e1b031787c5b47428ae04fd423d22b787be0f555daa0892ef65a8ee3a02a3c57","body":{"detail":"Measured with esbuild (minified, gzip -9) from the bridge source before and after commit 8a2ff314: eager bridge 5056 -> 5413 bytes, comment part 10766 -> 11644 bytes. Budgets are bridge 5501 and partComment 11821, recorded as measured size plus 10 percent, so both still fit, with under 200 bytes of headroom each. Not measured with scripts/bundle-size.mjs against a full npm run build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"015be019c0dd9e8ca33aafae42fbc53ff955e37b8a61197bc513fdb116f567da"},"summary":"The scroll report grows the eager bridge by about 360 bytes gzip, close to web/perf/bundle-budget.json","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
